#### Best Practice 5: Use SPIFFE IDs for Service Identity

**Guideline:** Include SPIFFE (Secure Production Identity Framework For Everyone) URIs in certificate SANs for standardized service identity.

```yaml
# Certificate with SPIFFE ID
apiVersion: cert-manager.io/v1
kind: Certificate
metadata:
  name: claims-api-cert
spec:
  secretName: claims-api-tls
  dnsNames:
    - claims-api.prod.svc.cluster.local
  uris:
    - spiffe://gainwell.com/ns/prod/sa/claims-api  # SPIFFE ID
```

```csharp
// Extract SPIFFE ID from certificate
string ExtractSpiffeId(X509Certificate2 cert)
{
    var san = cert.Extensions.OfType<X509SubjectAlternativeNameExtension>().FirstOrDefault();
    if (san != null)
    {
        foreach (var uri in san.EnumerateUniformResourceIdentifiers())
        {
            if (uri.StartsWith("spiffe://"))
                return uri;
        }
    }
    return null;
}
```

