#### Pitfall 2: Using Self-Signed Certificates Without Proper Validation

**Problem:** Self-signed certificates accepted without validating against internal CA, allowing impersonation.

**Solution:** Always validate certificate chain against internal CA.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD: Accept all self-signed certificates
handler.ServerCertificateCustomValidationCallback = (request, cert, chain, errors) =>
{
    return true;  // Accepts any certificate!
};

// ✅ GOOD: Validate against internal CA
handler.ServerCertificateCustomValidationCallback = (request, cert, chain, errors) =>
{
    if (errors == SslPolicyErrors.None)
        return true;

    // Load internal CA and validate
    var caCert = LoadInternalCACertificate();
    chain.ChainPolicy.ExtraStore.Add(caCert);

    return chain.Build(cert);
};
```

